Z||000000||JohnBoy||10-06-1999||04:51 PM||||I have a 1985 SE 6Cyl with a manual transmission.  I think I have the typical clutch problem, but a few things are different.  I cannot get the thing into first gear without pumping the clutch.  If I am excelerating hard, it does not go into third and makes a slight grinding noise.  It goes into third just fine at normal shifting speeds.  All other gears are fine.<P>If I let the clutch out all the way, I cannot jam the car into first gear, making the car move.  I can do this in second and third gingerly.  I Did not try fourth.  Sometimes it pops out of first when I do get it into the gear.<P>I think I have two possibly three problems:  First, the typical slave cylinder not extending properly (possible solution is ATF).  Second, I believe the synchro is wearing down for third gear.  And Third, possibly a synchro problem with first gear.<P>I would appreciate any comments.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||10-06-1999||09:07 PM||||Check the famous aluminum cluth pedal. These bend and wont give full travel to the master cylinder. Replace it with a steel one. Also if it pops out of gear its not the syncro its the gear.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-06-1999||09:23 PM||||did you check linkage adjustment? that will make it drop out of gear too.||||reg||1
